{"title":"Career Roadmap · Dental College Lecturer","role":"Dental College Lecturer","summary":"A Dental College Lecturer is an academic and clinical educator who teaches undergraduate dental students, supervises practical and clinical training, conducts research, prepares assessments, and contributes to academic activities within a dental institution.","facts":{"Current degree":"BDS (Bachelor of Dental Surgery)","Course":"Dental Surgery"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Dental College Lecturer is an academic and clinical educator who teaches undergraduate dental students, supervises practical and clinical training, conducts research, prepares assessments, and contributes to academic activities within a dental institution."},{"type":"p","text":"For this pathway, BDS is the foundation, but a teaching career in a dental college generally requires a recognized postgraduate dental qualification (MDS) in the relevant specialty, along with meeting the applicable regulatory and institutional requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical teaching areas correspond to dental specialties such as:"},{"type":"h","text":"Oral Medicine & Radiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery"},{"type":"h","text":"Conservative Dentistry & Endodontics"},{"type":"h","text":"Prosthodontics"},{"type":"h","text":"Periodontology"},{"type":"h","text":"Orthodontics & Dentofacial Orthopedics"},{"type":"h","text":"Pediatric & Preventive Dentistry"},{"type":"h","text":"Oral Pathology & Microbiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health Dentistry"},{"type":"h","text":"Prosthodontics and related specialty areas"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Exact faculty designation, eligibility, experience requirements, and promotion criteria can depend on current regulatory rules, institution type, and applicable notifications. Students should verify the latest requirements before applying."}]},{"headi